            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for to melt (something), then the Urdu for to plate (with metal)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: کھڑکھڑانا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کھڑکھڑانا — khaṛkhaṛānā — \"to rattle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ہوا میں کھڑکی کھڑکھڑاتی ہے۔ hawā meṅ khiṛkī khaṛkhaṛātī hai. The window rattles in the wind."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): وہ دروازہ کھڑکھڑایا, voh darvāzā khaṛkhaṛāyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کھڑکھڑانا (khaṛkhaṛānā) is inherited from Sanskrit khaṭakhaṭāyatē, \"crackles\", a word imitating the sound (CDIAL 3771)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
