          "title": "You'll want to know: قبضہ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قبضہ — qabzā — \"a hinge; possession (a hold on something)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دروازے کا ایک قبضہ ٹوٹ گیا۔ darvāze kā ek qabzā ṭūṭ gayā. One of the door's hinges has broken."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قبضہ (qabzā) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic qabḍa, \"a grip, a handle\"; Urdu also uses it for \"possession\", a hold on something, while the sense \"a hinge\" came later, and the sources we use do not show how it arose."
            }
          ]
        },
